.TH GIT-BRANCH-AUDIT 1 "2026-08-12" "git-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-branch-audit \- audit local branches against the default branch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git branch-audit
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git branch-audit
lists local branches with their state relative to the default branch: last
commit age, ahead/behind counts, whether they are merged into the default
branch, and the open pull request number when GitHub data is available.
.PP
The default branch is the reference point and is omitted from the listing. PR
lookup is best-effort: when
.B gh
is missing or unauthenticated the audit still reports local branch state and
omits PR numbers.
.PP
A branch counts as merged when its pinned tip is an ancestor of a pinned default
branch snapshot or exact replay evidence exists. For a squash merge, patch IDs
locate transitions on the default branch's first-parent history after the
branch merge base, including merge-commit transitions. The branch's raw net
delta must exactly equal the candidate's first-parent-to-commit delta. A later
mainline edit therefore does not erase an exact historical squash proof.
Multi-commit rebase and cherry-pick matches require every commit's patch ID and
the exact net delta in the pinned default snapshot. Raw comparisons include
full object IDs, types, modes, paths, and deletions, so
patch-ID-equivalent but byte-distinct content does not count as merged. This
applies to both the
.B merged
column and
.BR \-\-drop-merged .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-porcelain
Print stable tab-separated
.B branch
records:
.BR name ,
.B merged
(true/false),
.BR ahead ,
.BR behind ,
.B pr
number (may be empty),
.B committerdate
as a Unix timestamp, and
.B gone
(true/false for a deleted upstream).
.TP
.B \-\-drop-merged
Report exact local cleanup candidates already merged into the default branch,
including each branch's current object ID. No branch is deleted automatically:
Git has no portable primitive that serializes ref deletion with a checkout that
already resolved the branch. Branch enumeration must complete before reporting.
Requires
.B \-\-yes
unless
.B \-\-dry-run
is also used.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Confirm
.BR \-\-drop-merged .
.TP
.BI "\-b, \-\-base " branch
Use this branch as the default instead of inferring one.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry-run
Print candidate actions without changing anything.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Audit or cleanup completed.
.TP
.B 1
Audit or candidate reporting failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or local environment error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-cleanup-repo (1),
.BR git-repo-state (1),
.BR git-stash-audit (1)
